    "accepted_values": [
      {
        "locale": "quz",
        "key": "formats22_page_preview",
        "english": "Selected page preview",
        "proposed_value": "Aqllasqa raphipa qhawanapaqraq siq\\'in",
        "decision": "accept",
        "final_value": "Aqllasqa raphipa qhawanapaqraq siq\\'in",
        "confidence": "moderate independent model whole-phrase review, not native-human certification",
        "whole_phrase_reasoning": [
          "Aqlla-sqa modifies raphi as selected, not a selection imperative. Raphi-pa marks the selected page as genitive possessor. The head siq’i-n is image plus third-person possessive matching that possessor; it is not the accusative form siq’i-ta used in the unavailable sentence.",
          "Qhawa-na-paq-raq modifies the image as for preliminary viewing. Together the phrase denotes the preliminary-view image of the selected page. This is context-dependent descriptive preview terminology, not a claim that -raq alone means software preview.",
          "The complete singular possessive noun phrase fits the ImageView accessible description. It neither commands selection/opening nor announces successful loading or final import. The explicit image noun is supported by the visual consumer.",
          "Longer than the English but structurally coherent. Acceptance rests on the full modifier/possessor/possessed-head structure, not automatic extension of accepted navigation words or lexical token matches."
        ],
        "consumer_semantics": "PDF/TIFF showPages ImageView accessible name, not ICO or generic web pages. Description names the role while the image is cleared or loading/error status appears separately. Only the alive/current-generation preview result installs a bitmap; no success or permanence is promised.",
        "format_checks": {
          "NFC": true,
          "placeholder_count": 0,
          "newlines": 0,
          "single_Android_apostrophe_escape": true,
          "android_string_errors": [],
          "format_errors": []
        }
      },
      {
        "locale": "wo",
        "key": "ui_magnified_preview_ea9209",
        "english": "Magnified preview",
        "proposed_value": "Wonendi bi ñu màggal",
        "decision": "accept",
        "final_value": "Wonendi bi ñu màggal",
        "backtranslation": "The preview that is enlarged",
        "whole_phrase_reasoning": "Wonendi names the preliminary visual display. The b-class relative linker bi with the non-specific plural agent ñu and transitive enlargement verb màggal produces a descriptive relative clause, naturally read here as the preview which is enlarged. It is not an imperative to enable a feature and does not say the document dimensions have been enlarged. Relative-clause phrasing fits a dialog title for magnifier controls; it need not assert that the toggle is currently enabled. The nominal phrase is complete without an explicit copula or ellipsis. I accept the phrase as original Wolof composition at moderate model confidence, not as a source-attested whole phrase.",
        "confidence": "moderate independent whole-phrase model review",
        "runtime_assessment": "Title is selected only for showDrawingSettings(preview=true), whose controls toggle activeMagnifier and set previewMagnification. Renderer clips the preview lens and applies display scaling to the existing bitmap. Thus magnification concerns viewing, not a resampling/save operation or cursor-paint toggle. No success/permanence claim added.",
        "terminology_consistency": "Wonendi agrees with existing page-preview/error wording. The same-dialog toggle retains Seenu/seenub wording; this existing variation is explicitly left intact and is not certified as terminology uniformity. Synonymous preview wording does not change the proposed title’s function. Existing quoted toggle phrase is not a donor sentence or proof of grammar.",
